- A string is just a piece of text in programming-like a word, sentence, or even a whole paragraph
- there are three things to pay attention to in string:
    ^ Anything you'd type as words goes into a string: names, addresses, messages, etc
    ^ "Hello World" is a string containing those exact characters.
    ^ Double quotes are the markers

Example:
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
int main() {
  string myLetter = "I am 19 years old";
  cout << myLetter ;
return 0;
}

Explanation:
-If you input a string without a double wuotes at the star and end, the syntax will be error
